From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:25:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pbd: don't hand out StackAllocator's in-object buffer with
 libc++

PBD::StackAllocator keeps its buffer inside the allocator object, and
every copy (including rebinding copies) starts with a fresh, private
buffer. That only works as long as the container allocates and
deallocates through the very same allocator instance. Current libc++
(MSYS2 CLANG64) grows std::vector through a std::__split_buffer that
allocates via its own copy of the allocator; the vector later frees
that block through its own instance, which does not recognize the
pointer as one of its buffer slots and calls ::operator delete on stack
memory. Every PBD::Signal emission then corrupts the heap:

  SignalsTest::testEmission  warning: Critical error detected c0000374
  #3 ntdll!RtlFreeHeap
  #5 allocator_traits<PBD::StackAllocator<PBD::Connection*, 512>>::deallocate
  #6 vector<PBD::Connection*, PBD::StackAllocator<...>>::~vector
  #7 PBD::SignalWithCombiner<...>::operator()()

Fall back to heap allocation for all requests when building against
libc++. libstdc++ builds keep the stack fast path.
---
 libs/pbd/pbd/stack_allocator.h | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/pbd/pbd/stack_allocator.h b/libs/pbd/pbd/stack_allocator.h
index 859f244..f1f76b7 100644
--- a/libs/pbd/pbd/stack_allocator.h
+++ b/libs/pbd/pbd/stack_allocator.h
@@ -80,7 +80,19 @@ public:
 	/* inspired by http://howardhinnant.github.io/stack_alloc.h */
 	pointer allocate (size_type n, void* hint = 0)
 	{
+#ifdef _LIBCPP_VERSION
+		/* Recent libc++ containers allocate through temporary copies of
+		 * the allocator (e.g. in std::__split_buffer when a vector grows)
+		 * and later deallocate through the container's own instance.
+		 * Since every copy has its own in-object buffer, memory handed
+		 * out from a temporary's buffer would later be passed to
+		 * ::operator delete, corrupting the heap. Always use the heap
+		 * with libc++.
+		 */
+		if (false) {
+#else
 		if ((pointer)&_buf + stack_capacity >= _ptr + n) {
+#endif
 			DEBUG_STACK_ALLOC ("[%p] Allocate %ld item(s) of size %zu on the stack. used: %ld\n", (pointer)&_buf, n, sizeof (T), (_ptr - (pointer)&_buf));
 			pointer rv = _ptr;
 			_ptr += n;
